      "writtenOn": "2019-05-28T11:30:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s avoid doing some of this unnecessary work.\n\n  final NAI lockdownAgent \u003d getVpnAgentForUid(uid, true);\n  if (null \u003d\u003d lockdownAgent || !appliesToUid(uid)) return false;\n\n  final NAI vpnAgent \u003d getVpnAgentForUid(uid, false);\n  if (null \u003d\u003d vpnAgent || isConnected() || !appliesToUid(uid)) return false;\n\n  return true;\n\n\n\nOnce that\u0027s done, notice you will almost always return at the first return false. Therefore, you almost never call getVpnAgentForUid with a true argument, and in that case forLockdown \u003d\u003d forLockdown is almost always false and when it\u0027s true the other conditions in getVpnAgentForUid are almost always true. Therefore it becomes very advantageous to move that test first in the loop.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1883,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1898,
        "endChar": 21
      },
